dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.flow.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.semio.flow
start body
framing record

# P2 pilot (flow): REAL binary pack frame, replacing the old `serde_json::to_vec`-in-envelope
# shortcut (`📸️snapshot/🦀️component.rs`'s old `ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with`). `format u8` (real,
# fixed) then `schema_len`/`schema_bytes` (real, varint-length-prefixed UTF-8 — matches
# `write_str_lp`'s own wire exactly) are genuinely, fully described. Past that, `nodes`/`edges` are
# HOMOGENEOUS but variable-length repeated records (`FlowNode`/`FlowEdge`, each itself
# holding a further variable-length `params` sub-collection) — the `protocol-array-of-records` gap
# (`repeat`'s own arms are tag-dispatched, not "repeat N times, N from a count field", for an
# untagged homogeneous record): modeled as one opaque trailing `payload` chain, the same honest
# boundary every P1-P3 pilot's own nested/recursive payload uses. The real Rust
# `encode_flow_snapshot_binary`/`decode_flow_snapshot_binary` stays genuinely, fully
# structured (varint counts, per-field length-prefixes, real `f64` LE coordinates) — round-trip
# tested independently by this facet's own tests, only the protocol DESCRIPTION stops at this
# boundary.
header fixed 1
field format u8

segment schema_len varint
segment schema_bytes Array(u8, Field(schema_len))

chain payload bytes
